# Flowmates — copy to .env.local and fill in.
#
# Nothing here has a default. A build with an empty file has no cloud: local
# measurement, local vision and local reports all work; sign-in, sync and
# integrations report themselves unavailable. That is deliberate — see
# `apps/agent/src-tauri/src/sync_env.rs`.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_*, VITE_* and TAURI_* are read at build time and can end up inside
# the bundle. Public configuration only, never a secret.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Backend
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Base URL and public API key of your own backend. Until both are set, every
# cloud feature fails with a legible message instead of reaching a host.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=""
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=""

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Server-side secrets — never in the desktop build
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# These belong to the backend runtime, not to this repository and not to any
# build job that produces an application. They are listed for reference only:
#
#   the model provider key and endpoint used by the assistant
#   the model provider key used by written reports
#   the OAuth client secrets for issue-tracker integrations
#
# An OAuth *client id* is public and is used to build an authorization URL. A
# client *secret* is exchanged server-side, after the user's token has been
# verified. Never define a secret as a TAURI_ or VITE_ variable.

# Issue trackers — client ids only
TAURI_JIRA_CLIENT_ID=""
TAURI_LINEAR_CLIENT_ID=""

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Update signing
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The public counterpart is `plugins.updater.pubkey` in tauri.conf.json and is
# committed. The private key is not in this repository and its loss is final:
# no installed copy would ever accept an update again.
#
# Generate a pair with:
#   pnpm --filter @flowmates/mac exec tauri signer generate -w <path>
TAURI_SIGNING_PRIVATE_KEY=""
TAURI_SIGNING_PRIVATE_KEY_PASSWORD=""
